Each class has a unique representative of degree at most $n$, giving existence and uniqueness of $p$.
The preimages of the standard basis vectors are $\map {L_i} x = \displaystyle \prod_{j \mathop \ne i} \frac {x - x_j} {x_i - x_j}$, giving [[Lagrange Interpolation Formula|Lagrange's formula]] $p = \sum_i y_i L_i$.
{{qed}}
